	"notes": "Chapter 2 opening reuses the staffed clinical wing and existing prop markers. No Ward Zero access or new patient findings. Existing EHR remains available. Interview Room A seats Mara Ellis for her Scene 03 interview (Elias is back on the unit meanwhile); Elias returns once her records question is referred. Marcus Hale stands at the psychiatrist's office desk for Scene 06 once the analyst's next check is chosen (his own marker is in the security wing, unreachable in Chapter 2). A Facilities technician (unnamed, role only) stands at Interview Room A's door for Scene 07 once Hale's follow-up is requested. Scene 08: Hale's scene-only escorted pass (access_ward_entry, granted and returned through story options) opens the ward entry doors to the security corridor; the lift lobby doors are inspected from the corridor (story point on the camera dome in front of them). The lobby doors, lift, service hatch and W0-B keep their own access and stay locked. The nursing-station clock is the end-of-shift sign-out, so a completed Chapter 2 save can continue to Chapter 3.",
